<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Soporcel 1996 net drops yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Soporcel 1996 net drops yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan 1 to Dec 31 1996:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Net 0.3 vs 11.2</p>
<p>Sales 60.4 vs 76.0</p>
<p>Cash flow 13.9 vs 25.8</p>
<p>Note - Full company name is Soporcel-Sociedade Portuguesa de Celulose, a Portuguese pulp producer. &quot;The drop in profits reflects the depressed nature of the pulp sector, more evident in the first half of 1996,&quot; a statement said. &quot;In terms of demand for paper, the second half of 1996 was positive and showed a moderate recovery in prices.&quot; Soporcel said it raised pulp production by six percent year-on-year, paper production by 10 percent, and sales and productivity by nine percent.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom 351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
